+{
+  "archived_milestone": "2026.07.478",
+  "archived_research_roadmap_yaml": {
+    "content_before_activation": "milestone: 2026.07.479\nmilestone_title: ARTIFACT CREDIBILITY + CONTROLLED SELF-LEARNING + VERIFIER DECISION REPAIR\nmilestone_doc: openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md\ntasks:\n\n- id: exp5233-archive-478-activate-479\n  milestone: 2026.07.479\n  title: \"PHASE 0 transition -- archive .478 truth and activate .479\"\n  priority: critical\n  track: planning\n  deliverable: results/experiment_5233_archive_478_activate_479.json\n  operator_override: \"2026-05-29 operator directive: routine milestone-transition task; false-positive scope-match against prior archive/activate tasks is expected and authorized.\"\n  prior_failures:\n  - experiment_id: exp5220-archive-477-activate-478\n    verdict: \"complete: .477 archived and .478 activated; handoff preserves GAP-1 positive but unpromoted, GAP-4 flagged/protocol-blocked, MMLU hidden-state retired, self-learning memory written, ARC zero-delta, hardware reachability, and verifier-authenticity registry flags.\"\n    addressed_by: \"Routine milestone handoff for a new predecessor/successor pair (.478->.479); the deliverable is the current milestone archive and activation, not a rerun of .477->.478.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  agent_type: codex\n  model: gpt-5.5\n  max_turns: 30\n  estimated_wall_time_min: 25\n  prompt: |\n    CONTEXT:\n    Repo at {project_root}, run on or after {date}. All tasks in milestone 2026.07.478 have completed.\n    This is the standard transition task: archive .478 accurately, activate .479 by copying\n    research-roadmap-next.yaml into research-roadmap.yaml, and update operational docs. Do not turn blocked\n    or flagged evidence into headline claims.\n\n    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n    - research-roadmap.yaml (the .478 plan).\n    - openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md (the .479 design doc).\n    - ops/conductor-log.md entries for exp5220 through exp5232.\n    - ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md.\n    - results/experiment_5220_archive_477_activate_478.json through results/experiment_5232_capstone_v478.json.\n    - ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml.\n\n    TASK:\n    Write a precise .478 archive summary, activate the .479 roadmap, and leave the repo ready for the\n    conductor to execute exp5234 onward.\n\n    CONCRETE STEPS:\n    1. Read the .478 artifacts directly. Summarize the facts that matter for .479: GAP-1 blocked by subset\n       instability; GAP-4 canonical pool and clean validation blocked by adversarial QA flags; VerIbmc\n       solver feedback zero uplift but flagged for duration/methodology; typed multi-head memory\n       consumer-ready; ARC rubric usable but no patch; KAN tiny certificate produced; KV260 and PolarFire\n       reachable; GateMate still physical/JTAG blocked; no speedup claim.\n    2. Copy research-roadmap-next.yaml into research-roadmap.yaml exactly after preserving the old .478 plan\n       facts in the artifact summary.\n    3. Run the available roadmap activation checks against the activated research-roadmap.yaml, including\n       scripts/exclusion_manifest_lint.py and scripts/validate_prior_failures.py if present.\n    4. Update ops/status.md and ops/changelog.md with an append-only transition entry. Do not rewrite old\n       entries.\n    5. Confirm scripts/research_conductor.py was not modified.\n\n    REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:\n      v478_summary:\n        value: \"one paragraph with explicit exp5222/5224/5225/5226/5227/5228/5230/5231/5232 outcomes\"\n      research_roadmap_yaml_activated:\n        value: bool\n      exclusion_manifest_confirmed_clean:\n        value: bool\n      validation_commands_run:\n        value: \"list of commands and pass/fail\"\n      ops_docs_updated:\n        value: bool\n      research_conductor_py_untouched_confirmed:\n        value: bool\n      inference_substrate:\n        value: aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts\n      honest_verdict:\n        principle: \"Must start with complete:/complete_/success:/success_ and must state whether .479 was activated.\"\n\n    Run command, 'Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.'\n\n- id: exp5234-sota-ingestion-v479\n  milestone: 2026.07.479\n  title: \"PHASE 0 SOTA ingestion -- refresh 2025-2026 artifact QA, memory, KAN, hardware, and citation trail before execution\"\n  priority: high\n  track: research\n  deliverable: results/experiment_5234_sota_ingestion_v479.json\n  operator_override: \"CLAUDE.md SOTA-ingestion standing rule: every bleeding-edge milestone reserves a SOTA-ingestion slot; recurrence is expected and authorized.\"\n  prior_failures:\n  - experiment_id: exp5221-sota-ingestion-v478\n    verdict: \"complete: V478 SOTA refresh found no new actionable findings beyond the planning section; research-references.md unchanged; Semantic Scholar returned HTTP 429 for both EBT and ARM-EBM, so no fresh citation trail was inferred.\"\n    addressed_by: \"This is the required fresh .479 SOTA refresh after .478 completed; planning-time checks found new AgentCL/RW-EBR/FLaG/Fes/JANUS/KAN references and Semantic Scholar is reachable in this environment.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  agent_type: codex\n  model: gpt-5.5\n  max_turns: 40\n  estimated_wall_time_min: 40\n  prompt: |\n    CONTEXT:\n    Repo at {project_root}, run on or after {date}. The planning pass appended a V479 section to\n    research-references.md, but this reserved SOTA-ingestion task must re-check the freshest frontier\n    immediately before execution. Do not use /deep-research. Prefer primary sources: arXiv, OpenReview\n    pages, official project docs/repos, Extropic writing, Logical Intelligence posts, Hugging Face Papers,\n    GitHub repos, and Semantic Scholar metadata.\n\n    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n    - research-references.md (V478 and V479 sections).\n    - openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md (SOTA findings and phase plan).\n    - research-program.md (Continuous Self-Learning section).\n    - ops/exclusion