atch exists.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  - experiment_id: exp5216-arc-frontier-continuity-and-landmark-decomposition-v477\n    verdict: \"complete: ARC frontier continuity produced reproducible_total_levels_delta=0; no new live-path level banked.\"\n    addressed_by: \"This task tests a new live-agent-reachable patch with registry precheck and live_agent_self_discovery provenance instead of another continuity sweep.\"\n    retire_if_same_verdict: true\n  agent_type: codex\n  model: gpt-5.5\n  max_turns: 50\n  estimated_wall_time_min: 65\n  requires_gpu: true\n  prompt: |\n    CONTEXT:\n    Repo at {project_root}, run on or after {date}. This task runs only if exp5240 produced a tested live\n    patch candidate. The deliverable is live agent behavior under that patch, not an offline solve.\n\n    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:\n    - results/experiment_5240_arc_rubric_to_patch_synthesis_v479.json.\n    - ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml.\n    - python/carnot/arc/ live loop, registry, policy, and verifier routing modules.\n    - tests touching ARC live loop and the exp5240 patch.\n    - scripts/experiment_template.py and cached_sota_pair() if the live attempt invokes a model proposer.\n\n    TASK:\n    Run the patched ARC live path with strict provenance. If a level solve is claimed, it must be from the\n    live agent's own attempts and runtime reverse engineering. If no level is banked, record process deltas\n    and whether the patch should remain, roll back, or be iterated.\n\n    CONCRETE STEPS:\n    0. PRECONDITIONS: Apply or enable only the exp5240 patch. If using an LLM proposer, use cached_sota_pair()\n       and MODEL_SPECS with at least one mandated SOTA GGUF:\n       unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF, unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF, or\n       unsloth/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-GGUF.\n    1. Registry precheck: read ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml and do not target a duplicate level already\n       reproduced by the live mechanism.\n    2. Run the live agent with fixed see